# Backend secrets — real AWS/SonarQube/Jira credentials live here,
# never committed. Added 2026-09-05 when backend/ was created.
.env
**/.env
backend/__pycache__/
backend/**/__pycache__/

# Local data cache, all of it — Parquet files scripts/refresh_data.py
# writes from real CodeCommit data, its tracked_tickets.txt manifest, and
# services/s3_usage_service.py's developers_{1,30,90}d.csv snapshots.
# Regenerated automatically (refresh_data.py / POST /api/refresh[/{ticket}]
# for the Parquet files; any live GET /api/developers cache refresh for
# the CSVs) — not source, not shared between machines. The CSVs
# specifically hold REAL per-developer PII (names, emails, credit usage —
# see that module's own docstring on why they're human-readable) rather
# than credentials, but belong in the same "never committed" category as
# backend/.env for the same reason: whoever clones this repo fresh should
# get their own real data, not a snapshot of someone else's. Widened from
# two narrower rules (`*.parquet` + `tracked_tickets.txt` only) to the
# whole directory 2026-09-09 after confirming, while auditing this repo
# before a push, that the CSVs above were the one thing in this directory
# those two narrower rules didn't actually cover.
backend/data/

# Local Kiro session state — never shared, resets per branch
.kiro/current-ticket.json

# A ticket typed at post-commit's ticket-switch prompt that couldn't be
# validated against Jira at the git-hook level (no credential there) —
# Kiro chat's ask-ticket hook checks it for real via atlassian-rovo MCP
# on the next message, then deletes this file. (pre-commit's own
# manual-entry fallback, which used to write this too, was removed
# entirely 2026-08-27 — it no longer prompts the terminal at all.)
# See TODO.md, 2026-08-27.
.kiro/pending-ticket-check.json

# Same category as pending-ticket-check.json above — a transient marker
# the ask-ticket hook writes while mid a "did you mean X?" or "please
# refresh credits" sub-dialogue, so the fast-path command hook knows to
# stand down. Deleted by the agent hook once that sub-flow concludes.
# Added 2026-08-31 alongside the marker itself — this .gitignore entry
# was missing from that same change until this repo-verification pass
# caught it (confirmed live: nothing else ignored it, so it could have
# been committed by an ordinary `git add -A` mid-conversation).
.kiro/pending-baseline-confirm.json

# docs/kiro-confirmed-persistent-signal-proposal.md — append-only,
# command-hook-only log of when candidate ticket IDs were first
# detected, used to compute Kiro-Confirmed's gap-seconds. Local,
# per-machine, not tracking data itself (the real record is the
# Kiro-Confirmed trailer on each commit). Same class of omission as
# pending-baseline-confirm.json above, caught the same way — asked
# directly whether this file was gitignored, checked, found it wasn't.
.kiro/candidate-detection-log.jsonl

# Session-start greeting marker (aidlc-session-greeting.json) — same
# transient, gitignored-marker category as pending-ticket-check.json
# and pending-baseline-confirm.json above, and the same omission
# class: found sitting untracked-but-not-ignored on disk from a real
# live session while investigating an unrelated bug report, 2026-09-04
# — never added when the file itself was introduced 2026-09-02. Same
# accidental-commit risk as candidate-detection-log.jsonl already hit
# for real (see TODO.md).
.kiro/pending-session-greeting.json

# Sonar scan scratch output
/tmp/sonar-scan.log

# .kiro-tracking/ — hook diagnostic log plus one debug-convenience JSON
# file per ticket (overwritten every commit, never accumulated). Neither
# is the tracking data anymore: as of 2026-08-27 the real record is each
# commit's own Kiro-* trailers (see .githooks/commit-msg), which
# scripts/calculate-pr-credits.sh reads from git history directly.
# Previously this held one *committed* JSON file per commit forever —
# removed after confirming (grep) nothing but commit-msg ever read them.
# See TODO.md and docs/runbook.md.
.kiro-tracking/

# Internal demo/handover artifact — lists real (non-secret) infra
# identifiers (AWS account IDs, the real S3 bucket name, the real
# CodeCommit repo name) that don't need to leave this machine, especially
# once this repo is pushed somewhere public. Generated by
# scripts/generate_handover_doc.py, which itself stays tracked (it's just
# code) — only its output is excluded here.
Vantage_Project_Handover.docx

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Local Claude Code settings — machine-specific, not project config
.claude/
